# Issue #1087: both ends behind symmetric NATs (libwebrtc's test NAT rules, #985), where no direct pair can work,
# so the call relays through the emulated TURN server (TURN over UDP, iceTransportPolicy relay). The media crosses
# the same links as clean_link's, with the ChannelData header added to each packet.
name ice_symmetric_nat_turn
describe Both ends behind symmetric NATs, relayed through TURN over UDP, on clean_link's link (transport ice, #1087)
transport ice
compare off
nat symmetric
turn udp
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
expect setup.connected == 1
expect transport.send_failures == 0
expect transport.local_candidate_type == 3
expect transport.remote_candidate_type == 3
expect transport.relay_protocol == 1
expect audio.concealed_pct < 1
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect video.freeze_count == 0
expect video.render_fps >= 29
